== External Links == - [Kamitonda Town Cultural Property Classroom Series](http://www.town.kamitonda.lg.jp/section/kami50y/kami50y.html)
== Cultural Significance == These shrines represent the fusion of Shinto and Buddhist practices unique to Kumano Pilgrimage culture. Many are associated with legends, poetry, and historical figures, such as {{ill|Fujiwara no Teika|ja|藤原定家|qq=draft}} and {{ill|Izumi Shikibu|ja|和泉式部|qq=draft}}.
